---
const photographs = [
  { date: '2026-08-19', label: '19 August 2026', shortLabel: '19 AUG 2026', image: '/media/photo-incubation-2026-08-19.webp' },
  { date: '2026-08-27', label: '27 August 2026', shortLabel: '27 AUG 2026', image: '/media/photo-incubation-2026-08-27.webp' },
  { date: '2026-09-04', label: '4 September 2026', shortLabel: '04 SEP 2026', image: '/media/photo-incubation-2026-09-04.webp' },
];

const phases = [
  {
    id: 'incubation',
    number: '01',
    name: 'Incubation',
    title: 'Much of the work happens out of sight.',
    description: 'Mycelium spreads through the straw inside each bag. What is visible on the surface is only part of the story, so a quiet-looking bag does not tell us everything about colonization.',
    focus: 'Observe patiently. Follow the developing mycelium and the surrounding conditions.',
    image: '/media/cultivation/stage-incubation.webp',
    alt: 'Rendered illustration of a hanging bag of chopped straw in clear plastic, with white mycelium beginning to spread through it.',
  },
  {
    id: 'pinning',
    number: '02',
    name: 'Pinning',
    title: 'The first small signs become visible.',
    description: 'Tiny mushroom initials mark a visible transition. This is a useful moment to look closely at the relationship between the growing environment and what the cameras can actually observe.',
    focus: 'Look for the transition. Environmental settings and observation schedules can change by phase.',
    image: '/media/cultivation/stage-pinning.webp',
    alt: 'Rendered illustration of the same bag, now white with mycelium, with clusters of tiny grey-tipped mushroom pins at three cuts in the plastic.',
  },
  {
    id: 'fruiting',
    number: '03',
    name: 'Fruiting & growth',
    title: 'Slow changes start to take shape.',
    description: 'Oyster mushrooms develop into their recognizable clusters. Scheduled photographs can make gradual changes easier to see, while environmental measurements provide a separate record in Grafana.',
    focus: 'Observe shape and development. A visual impression alone is not a measurement of yield.',
    image: '/media/cultivation/stage-fruiting.webp',
    alt: 'Rendered illustration of the bag with grey-brown oyster mushroom clusters growing from its three openings.',
  },
  {
    id: 'harvest',
    number: '04',
    name: 'Harvest',
    title: 'An endpoint, and a new set of questions.',
    description: 'Harvest offers a moment to document the outcome and review the run. Any conclusions need to account for the actual observations, the conditions, and the gaps in the record.',
    focus: 'Reflect on the evidence. This conceptual stage does not indicate that a harvest has been completed.',
    image: '/media/cultivation/stage-harvest.webp',
    alt: 'Rendered illustration of the bag with cut stems at its openings and the harvested oyster clusters in a dish below; not evidence of an actual harvest.',
  },
];


---

<div class="research-chapters" data-research-chapters>
  <section id="experiment" class="rc-section rc-experiment" aria-labelledby="experiment-heading">
    <div class="rc-container">
      <div class="rc-section-label"><span class="rc-marker"></span> THE EXPERIMENT <span class="rc-label-rule"></span> FIELD NOTES / 01</div>
      <div class="rc-experiment-grid">
        <div class="rc-experiment-copy">
          <h2 id="experiment-heading">A small environment.<br /><em>A bigger question.</em></h2>
          <p class="rc-lead">What can we learn when we make the growing environment observable?</p>
          <p>Smart Mushroom Hub brings oyster mushroom cultivation, environmental sensing, and a little automation into one carefully observed space. A Raspberry Pi connects the physical experiment to its digital record.</p>
          <p>The tent is compared with the surrounding room as an <strong>environmental reference</strong>. Ventilation, humidification, and lighting can be adjusted by phase. The aim is to understand the system as it runs, and document what it teaches us.</p>
          <dl class="rc-experiment-facts">
            <div><dt>THE SPECIES</dt><dd>Oyster mushrooms</dd></div>
            <div><dt>THE SUBSTRATE</dt><dd>Pasteurized straw</dd></div>
            <div><dt>THE FIRST RUN</dt><dd>Incubation began<br />28 July 2026</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
        <figure class="rc-hardware-figure">
          <div class="rc-photo-wrap"><img src="/media/hardware-setup.webp" alt="The project's physical electronics and hardware setup." loading="lazy" width="900" height="1100" /></div>
          <figcaption><span>01 / FROM THE WORKBENCH</span><span>Real hardware. An ongoing experiment.</span></figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="cultivation" class="rc-section rc-cultivation" aria-labelledby="cultivation-heading">
    <div class="rc-container">
      <div class="rc-section-label"><span class="rc-marker"></span> THE CULTIVATION CYCLE <span class="rc-label-rule"></span> EXPLORE THE PHASES</div>
      <div class="rc-section-intro">
        <h2 id="cultivation-heading">Growth has<br /><em>its own rhythm.</em></h2>
        <p>The needs of a living system change as it develops. These are conceptual stages of cultivation, with different reasons to observe, illuminate, humidify, or ventilate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rc-phase-explorer" data-phase-explorer>
        <div class="rc-phase-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Conceptual cultivation stages" hidden>
          {phases.map((phase, index) => (
            <button type="button" class="rc-phase-tab" id={`rc-tab-${phase.id}`} role="tab" aria-selected={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls={`rc-panel-${phase.id}`} tabindex={index === 0 ? 0 : -1} data-phase-tab>
              <span class="rc-tab-number">{phase.number}</span><span>{phase.name}</span><span class="rc-tab-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </button>
          ))}
        </div>
        {phases.map((phase) => (
          <div class="rc-phase-panel" id={`rc-panel-${phase.id}`} role="region" aria-labelledby={`rc-stage-title-${phase.id}`} data-phase-panel>
            <div class="rc-phase-content">
              <p class="rc-kicker">STAGE {phase.number} / {phase.name.toUpperCase()}</p>
              <h3 id={`rc-stage-title-${phase.id}`}>{phase.title}</h3>
              <p>{phase.description}</p>
              <p class="rc-phase-focus"><span aria-hidden="true">↳</span>{phase.focus}</p>
            </div>
            <figure class="rc-phase-art">
              <span class="rc-art-ring rc-art-ring-one" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="rc-art-ring rc-art-ring-two" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <img src={phase.image} alt={phase.alt} width="780" height="1080" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <figcaption>RENDERED ILLUSTRATION · CONCEPTUAL, NOT AN OBSERVED RESULT</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
        ))}
        <p class="rc-phase-note">Explore the stages in any order. This is a guide to the growing process, not a current phase indicator.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>



  <section id="observations" class="rc-section rc-observations" aria-labelledby="observations-heading">
    <div class="rc-container">
      <div class="rc-section-label"><span class="rc-marker"></span> CAMERA & TIMELAPSE <span class="rc-label-rule"></span> A DIFFERENT TIMESCALE</div>
      <div class="rc-observation-grid">
        <div class="rc-photo-viewer" data-photo-viewer>
          {photographs.map((photo, index) => (
            <figure class="rc-capture" id={`rc-capture-${photo.date}`} data-capture>
              <a href={photo.image} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={`Open the controlled tent photograph from ${photo.label} in a new tab`}>
                <img src={photo.image} alt={`Real camera photograph from ${photo.label}: straw-filled substrate bags hanging from the PVC frame inside the controlled tent.`} width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" />
                <span class="rc-image-expand" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
              </a>
              <figcaption><span><span class="rc-capture-number">0{index + 1}</span><time datetime={photo.date}>{photo.label}</time></span><span>INCUBATION · CONTROLLED TENT</span></figcaption>
            </figure>
          ))}
          <div class="rc-photo-thumbnails" role="group" aria-label="Choose a published photograph" hidden data-photo-controls>
            {photographs.map((photo, index) => (
              <button type="button" class="rc-photo-thumb" aria-label={`Show photograph from ${photo.label}`} aria-pressed={index === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls={`rc-capture-${photo.date}`} data-photo-button data-photo-label={photo.label}>
                <img src={photo.image} alt="" width="320" height="180" loading="lazy" /><span>{photo.shortLabel}</span>
              </button>
            ))}
          </div>
          <p class="rc-photo-context">Source: controlled-camera captures from the first cultivation experiment. Dates shown in Cairo time (UTC+3).</p>
          <p class="rc-sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-photo-announcement></p>
        </div>
        <div class="rc-observation-copy">
          <h2 id="observations-heading">A record of<br /><em>slow change.</em></h2>
          <p class="rc-lead">Some changes are easier to see when you give them time.</p>
          <p>These photographs come from the controlled tent during incubation. They show the bags and their surroundings at three selected moments, without turning a visual impression into a growth claim.</p>
          <div class="rc-media-types">
            <div><span class="rc-small-number">01</span><div><h3>Still photographs</h3><p>Individual moments, with dates and context.</p></div></div>
            <div><span class="rc-small-number">02</span><div><h3>Produced timelapses</h3><p>A sequence of observations, brought together.</p></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="rc-camera-note"><img src="/media/camera.webp" alt="Illustration of the Raspberry Pi camera module." width="76" height="96" loading="lazy" /><p>The cameras take scheduled stills, with capture schedules that change by cultivation phase. This is a published selection, not a live camera feed.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rc-timelapse">
        <div class="rc-timelapse-copy">
          <p class="rc-kicker">THE INCUBATION SEQUENCE</p>
          <h3>18 days,<br /><em>in 12 seconds.</em></h3>
          <p>The same tent, photographed over 18 days. This silent sequence brings 73 scheduled incubation stills together.</p>
          <p id="rc-timelapse-description">Hanging substrate bags remain in view as the camera records the interior of the tent. The film shows the captured sequence, without generated frames.</p>
          <a href="/media/incubation-controlled-2026-08-18-to-09-05.mp4" download>Download the film <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <figure class="rc-timelapse-film">
          <video controls playsinline preload="none" poster="/media/photo-incubation-2026-08-19.webp" width="1280" height="720" aria-label="Silent timelapse of the controlled tent during incubation" aria-describedby="rc-timelapse-description">
            <source src="/media/incubation-controlled-2026-08-18-to-09-05.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
            <p>Your browser cannot play this video. <a href="/media/incubation-controlled-2026-08-18-to-09-05.mp4">Download the incubation timelapse.</a></p>
          </video>
          <figcaption>73 scheduled stills · 18 Aug-5 Sep 2026 · Controlled tent</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="vision" class="rc-section rc-vision" aria-labelledby="vision-heading">
    <div class="rc-container">
      <div class="rc-section-label"><span class="rc-marker"></span> COMPUTER VISION <span class="rc-label-rule"></span> RESEARCH IN PROGRESS</div>
      <div class="rc-vision-grid">
        <div class="rc-vision-copy">
          <h2 id="vision-heading">From looking<br /><em>to recognizing.</em></h2>
          <p class="rc-lead">Can a camera help us observe mushrooms more consistently?</p>
          <p>A YOLOv8s model has been trained to detect mushrooms. The next ambition is to bring inference onto the Raspberry Pi using the Hailo-10H accelerator, then examine what the detections can reliably tell us.</p>
          <p class="rc-vision-principle">A detection is an observation.<br />It is not, by itself, a growth measurement.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rc-vision-work">
          <div class="rc-vision-step">
            <span class="rc-vision-index">01</span>
            <div><p class="rc-vision-status">TRAINED</p><h3>A mushroom detector</h3><p>YOLOv8s, with mushroom as the primary class. The reported model result is <strong>mAP50 ≈ 0.9443</strong>.</p><p class="rc-vision-caveat">Evaluation-set details are not supplied here, so this figure does not establish performance in the tent.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="rc-vision-step">
            <span class="rc-vision-index">02</span>
            <div><p class="rc-vision-status rc-status-planned">PLANNED INTEGRATION</p><h3>Inference at the edge</h3><p>The Raspberry Pi AI HAT 2 is intended to run the model locally. A complete deployed inference workflow is not yet demonstrated here.</p></div>
          </div>
          <div class="rc-vision-step">
            <span class="rc-vision-index">03</span>
            <div><p class="rc-vision-status rc-status-planned">FUTURE WORK</p><h3>From detections to evidence</h3><p>Publish real annotated examples, inspect errors, and investigate whether visible counts or area can support useful observations over time.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rc-vision-footnote"><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><p>Annotated predictions will appear here when actual outputs are ready to share. No demonstration detections are presented as experiment results.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>


</div>

<script>
  const initializeResearchChapters = () => {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-phase-explorer]').forEach((explorer) => {
      if (explorer.dataset.initialized === 'true') return;
      const tabs = Array.from(explorer.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-phase-tab]'));
      const panels = Array.from(explorer.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-phase-panel]'));
      const tablist = explorer.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[role="tablist"]');
      if (!tablist || !tabs.length || tabs.length !== panels.length) return;
      const selectTab = (selectedIndex: number, moveFocus = false) => {
        tabs.forEach((tab, index) => {
          const selected = index === selectedIndex;
          tab.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(selected));
          tab.tabIndex = selected ? 0 : -1;
          if (panels[index]) panels[index].hidden = !selected;
        });
        if (moveFocus) tabs[selectedIndex]?.focus();
      };
      tabs.forEach((tab, index) => {
        panels[index].setAttribute('role', 'tabpanel');
        panels[index].setAttribute('aria-labelledby', tab.id);
        panels[index].tabIndex = 0;
        tab.addEventListener('click', () => selectTab(index));
        tab.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
          let nextIndex: number | undefined;
          if (event.key === 'ArrowRight') nextIndex = (index + 1) % tabs.length;
          if (event.key === 'ArrowLeft') nextIndex = (index - 1 + tabs.length) % tabs.length;
          if (event.key === 'Home') nextIndex = 0;
          if (event.key === 'End') nextIndex = tabs.length - 1;
          if (nextIndex !== undefined) {
            event.preventDefault();
            selectTab(nextIndex, true);
          }
        });
      });
      selectTab(0);
      tablist.hidden = false;
      explorer.dataset.initialized = 'true';
    });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-photo-viewer]').forEach((viewer) => {
      if (viewer.dataset.initialized === 'true') return;
      const figures = Array.from(viewer.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-capture]'));
      const buttons = Array.from(viewer.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-photo-button]'));
      const controls = viewer.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-photo-controls]');
      const announcement = viewer.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-photo-announcement]');
      if (!controls || !buttons.length || buttons.length !== figures.length) return;
      const selectPhoto = (selectedIndex: number, announce = true) => {
        buttons.forEach((button, index) => {
          const selected = index === selectedIndex;
          button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(selected));
          figures[index].hidden = !selected;
        });
        if (announce && announcement) announcement.textContent = `Showing the controlled tent photograph from ${buttons[selectedIndex].dataset.photoLabel}.`;
      };
      buttons.forEach((button, index) => button.addEventListener('click', () => selectPhoto(index)));
      selectPhoto(0, false);
      controls.hidden = false;
      viewer.dataset.initialized = 'true';
    });
  };
  initializeResearchChapters();
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', initializeResearchChapters);
</script>

<style>
  .research-chapters { --rc-ink: #172b29; --rc-muted: #60665b; --rc-paper: #f6f3eb; --rc-olive: #6f7957; --rc-orange: #d45b36; color: var(--rc-ink); background: var(--rc-paper); font-family: var(--font-body, sans-serif); }
  .rc-section { padding-block: clamp(76px, 8vw, 128px); scroll-margin-top: 86px; }
  .rc-container { width: min(var(--page-width), calc(100% - 2 * var(--page-pad, 5vw))); margin-inline: auto; }
  .rc-section-label { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .12em; line-height: 1.5; }
  .rc-marker { width: 6px; height: 6px; flex: 0 0 6px; background: var(--rc-orange); }
  .rc-label-rule { height: 1px; flex: 1; background: currentColor; opacity: .18; margin-inline: 12px; }
  h2, h3, p, figure { margin: 0; }
  h2 { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: clamp(40px, 4.65vw, 65px); line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -.045em; text-wrap: balance; }
  h2 em { font-weight: 400; color: var(--rc-olive); }
  p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.85; color: var(--rc-muted); }
  p + p { margin-top: 17px; }
  p strong { color: var(--rc-ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .rc-lead { color: var(--rc-ink); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .rc-kicker { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .12em; line-height: 1.5; }
  .rc-experiment-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr; align-items: center; gap: clamp(44px, 8vw, 116px); margin-top: 65px; }
  .rc-experiment-copy h2 { margin-bottom: 29px; }
  .rc-experiment-copy .rc-lead { max-width: 420px; margin-bottom: 19px; }
  .rc-experiment-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin: 32px 0 0; padding-top: 25px; border-top: 1px solid #172b2926; }
  .rc-experiment-facts dt { font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .1em; color: var(--rc-muted); margin-bottom: 9px; }
  .rc-experiment-facts dd { font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .rc-photo-wrap { height: 525px; overflow: hidden; background: #e4e1d8; }
  .rc-photo-wrap img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: center; display: block; }
  .rc-hardware-figure figcaption { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; margin-top: 15px; font-size: 9px; color: var(--rc-muted); line-height: 1.6; }
  .rc-hardware-figure figcaption span:first-child { letter-spacing: .08em; }
  .rc-cultivation { background: #ebece2; }
  .rc-section-intro { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 70px; align-items: end; margin-top: 58px; margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .rc-section-intro > p { max-width: 440px; padding-bottom: 4px; }
  .rc-phase-tabs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); border-bottom: 1px solid #172b292b; }
  .rc-phase-tabs[hidden] { display: none; }
  .rc-phase-explorer:not([data-initialized="true"]) .rc-phase-panel + .rc-phase-panel { border-top: 1px solid #172b292b; }
  .rc-phase-tab { appearance: none; border: 0; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; background: transparent; margin-bottom: -1px; display: flex; align-items: center; text-align: left; gap: 15px; padding: 20px 18px 20px 0; font: inherit; font-size: 13px; color: #5c6558; cursor: pointer; transition: color .2s, border-color .2s; min-height: 62px; }
  .rc-tab-number { font-size: 10px; color: var(--rc-olive); }
  .rc-tab-arrow { margin-left: auto; font-size: 20px; opacity: 0; transform: translate(-4px, 4px); transition: opacity .2s, transform .2s; }
  .rc-phase-tab[aria-selected="true"] { color: var(--rc-ink); border-color: var(--rc-orange); }
  .rc-phase-tab[aria-selected="true"] .rc-tab-number { color: var(--rc-orange); }
  .rc-phase-tab[aria-selected="true"] .rc-tab-arrow { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  .rc-phase-tab:hover { color: var(--rc-orange); }
  .rc-phase-tab:focus-visible, .rc-phase-panel:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--rc-orange); outline-offset: 5px; }
  .rc-phase-panel { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 60px; min-height: 470px; padding-top: 18px; }
  .rc-phase-panel[hidden] { display: none; }
  .rc-phase-content { max-width: 470px; padding-block: 32px; }
  .rc-phase-content .rc-kicker { color: var(--rc-olive); margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .rc-phase-content h3 { font-family: var(--font-display, Georgia, serif); font-size: clamp(29px, 3.1vw, 43px); line-height: 1.1; font-weight: 400; letter-spacing: -.03em; margin-bottom: 23px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .rc-phase-focus { display: flex; gap: 14px; border-top: 1px solid #172b2920; padding-top: 20px; margin-top: 26px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--rc-ink); }
  .rc-phase-focus span { color: var(--rc-orange); font-size: 23px; line-height: 1; }
  .rc-phase-art { position: relative; height: 430px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; isolation: isolate; }
  .rc-phase-art img { display: block; width: 260px; max-width: 78%; height: 360px; object-fit: contain; position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .rc-art-ring { width: 270px; height: 270px; border: 1px solid #76815f26; border-radius: 50%; position: absolute; pointer-events: none; }
  .rc-art-ring-two { width: 370px; height: 370px; border-color: #76815f15; }
  .rc-phase-art figcaption { position: absolute; bottom: 0; text-align: center; font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .06em; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--rc-muted); }
  .rc-phase-note { border-top: 1px solid #172b2920; margin-top: 25px; padding-top: 17px; font-size: 11px; }
  .rc-observation-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.3fr .85fr; gap: clamp(40px, 6vw, 85px); align-items: center; margin-top: 60px; }
  .rc-capture[hidden], .rc-photo-thumbnails[hidden] { display: none; }
  .rc-capture > a { display: block; position: relative; background: #e4e6dd; }
  .rc-capture > a > img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover; }
  .rc-capture figcaption { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 15px; margin-top: 15px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .rc-capture figcaption > span:first-child { font-size: 12px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 15px; }
  .rc-capture-number { font-size: 9px; color: var(--rc-olive); }
  .rc-capture figcaption > span:last-child { font-size: 8px; color: var(--rc-muted); letter-spacing: .06em; text-align: right; }
  .rc-image-expand { position: absolute; display: grid; place-items: center; bottom: 12px; right: 12px; width: 35px; height: 35px; background: var(--rc-paper); color: var(--rc-ink); font-size: 22px; transition: background .2s; }
  .rc-capture a:hover .rc-image-expand { background: #dce0cf; }
  .rc-photo-thumbnails { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin-top: 30px; }
  .rc-photo-thumb { appearance: none; border: 0; border-bottom: 2px solid transparent; padding: 0 0 12px; font: inherit; background: transparent; color: var(--rc-muted); cursor: pointer; text-align: left; }
  .rc-photo-thumb img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; object-fit: cover; opacity: .65; transition: opacity .2s; }
  .rc-photo-thumb span { display: block; font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .05em; margin-top: 10px; }
  .rc-photo-thumb[aria-pressed="true"] { border-color: var(--rc-orange); color: var(--rc-ink); }
  .rc-photo-thumb[aria-pressed="true"] img, .rc-photo-thumb:hover img { opacity: 1; }
  .rc-photo-thumb:focus-visible, .rc-capture a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--rc-orange); outline-offset: 5px; }
